      "writtenOn": "2024-03-06T16:04:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "vdonnefort@google.com I am a bit worried that this field is host controlled. Eg. someone can trick the hyp into allocating 1 page but they can specify more pages in the `pgd_pages` (eg. 3) field which can pass this check. If the `required_pgd_len` is 2 pages then we end up overflowing one page.\n\nAn attacker can overwrite host kernel memory with this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2633,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2633,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "087f3c1e68b34dc5e8b60195a961e8862fafd028",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84753a30_8601e49d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2633,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T09:20:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought when you host_donate_hyp the memory for the snapshot, you were using the hyp internal function to get the PGD size anyway? \n\nIf that\u0027s the case, this field here is just a simple check. It doesn\u0027t give any surface for the host to attack the hypervisor.\n\nIf the wrong PGD size is given, the hyp will lock what it thinks is the PGD size (and fails if it is not allowed to).",
      "parentUuid": "603d6187_e71f9434",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2633,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2633,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "087f3c1e68b34dc5e8b60195a961e8862fafd028",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29a57b02_ba7da3f2",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2633,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T15:57:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if it gives the correct PGD size but on the other side it passes a smaller PGD buffer ?",
      "parentUuid": "84753a30_8601e49d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2633,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2633,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "087f3c1e68b34dc5e8b60195a961e8862fafd028",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "edc9a4da_e1efd1d0",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/mem_protect.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2633,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T17:16:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The hypervisor would just write in those buffers.\n\nWhat matters is that the hypervisor will not write on anything that isn\u0027t owned by the host.",
      "parentUuid": "29a57b02_ba7da3f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2633,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2633,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "087f3c1e68b34dc5e8b60195a961e8862fafd028",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
