        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T16:33:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`The back and forth with pkvm.c is a bit strange.` - I agree, I had to do that because `pkvm.c` has the knowledge about the handles.\n\nNow I have :\n```\nhyp_main.c  |  mem_protect.c   |  ../nvhe/pkvm.c  | mem_protect.c\nhandler     -\u003e  __pkvm_stage2_snapshot\n                               -\u003e  pkvm_stage2_snapshot_by_handle\n                                                  -\u003e __pkvm_guest_stage2_snapshot\n```\n\nand with your suggestion it will become:\n\n```\nhyp_main.c  | ../nvhe/pkvm.c  | mem_protect.c\nhandler     -\u003e  __pkvm_stage2_snapshot_by_handle\n                                                  -\u003e __pkvm_guest_stage2_snapshot\n```\n\nI guest this should work, but we will have to duplicate the call to `pkvm_setup_snapshot` and `pkvm_teardown_snapshot` for the host. On the other hand the call chain will be more clear with your suggestion.",
      "parentUuid": "8cef89b5_2cba8118",
      "revId": "087f3c1e68b34dc5e8b60195a961e8862fafd028",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
